Bootstrap: docker
From: ubuntu:22.04

%labels
    Author      Benjamin Zelvelder
    Version     1.2.0
    Description Genome Alignment Based Bait Inference (GABBI): A fully automated probe design pipeline
                based on whole-genome alignments for target capture phylogenomics

%help
    
    GABBI — Genome Alignment-Based Bait Inference pipeline
    ======================================================

    This pipeline requires Singularity >= 3.8 or Apptainer >= 1.0

    To view detailed options of the GABBI pipeline, run:
        singularity run GABBI_v1.2.0.sif --help

    If you want to build the singularity image manually using the definition file, run:
        singularity build --fakeroot GABBI_v1.2.0.sif GABBI_v1.2.0.def

    If you are using the GABBI pipeline, please cite the GABBI publication:
	- B. Zelvelder, L. Benoit, A. Loiseau, J. Haran, R. Allio (2026) A new method based on genome alignments provides a highly resolutive target enrichment set for weevils (Coleoptera, Curculionoidea). bioRxiv 2026.05.09.724036. (https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.05.09.724036)

    And tools used by the GABBI pipeline:
	- AMAS: Borowiec ML. 2016 AMAS: a fast tool for alignment manipulation and computing of summary statistics. PeerJ 4, e1660. (https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.1660)
	- BLAST+ suite: Camacho C, Coulouris G, Avagyan V, Ma N, Papadopoulos J, Bealer K, Madden TL. 2009 BLAST+: architecture and applications. BMC Bioinformatics 10, 421. (https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2105-10-421)
	- Cactus: Armstrong J et al. 2020 Progressive Cactus is a multiple-genome aligner for the thousand-genome era. Nature 587, 246–251. (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-2871-y)
	- GNU Parallel: Tange O. 2011 GNU Parallel - The Command-Line Power Tool. login: The USENIX Magazine, 42-47.
	- HmmCleaner: Di Franco A, Poujol R, Baurain D, Philippe H. 2019 Evaluating the usefulness of alignment filtering methods to reduce the impact of errors on evolutionary inferences. BMC Evol Biol 19, 21. (https://doi.org/10.1186/s12862-019-1350-2)
	- IQTREE3: Wong T et al. 2025 IQ-TREE 3: Phylogenomic Inference Software using Complex Evolutionary Models. (https://doi.org/10.32942/X2P62N)
	- MACSE v2: Ranwez V, Douzery EJP, Cambon C, Chantret N, Delsuc F. 2018 MACSE v2: Toolkit for the Alignment of Coding Sequences Accounting for Frameshifts and Stop Codons. Molecular Biology and Evolution 35, 2582–2584. (https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msy159)
	- MafFilter: Dutheil JY, Gaillard S, Stukenbrock EH. 2014 MafFilter: a highly flexible and extensible multiple genome alignment files processor. BMC Genomics 15, 53. (https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2164-15-53)
	- MAFFT: Katoh K, Standley DM. 2013 MAFFT Multiple Sequence Alignment Software Version 7: Improvements in performance and usability. Molecular Biology and Evolution 30, 772–780. (https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/mst010)
	- OMM_MACSE pipeline: Scornavacca C, Belkhir K, Lopez J, Dernat R, Delsuc F, Douzery EJP, Ranwez V. 2019 OrthoMaM v10: Scaling-Up Orthologous Coding Sequence and Exon Alignments with More than One Hundred Mammalian Genomes. Molecular Biology and Evolution 36, 861–862. (https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msz015)
	- PHAST: Hubisz MJ, Pollard KS, Siepel A. 2011 PHAST and RPHAST: phylogenetic analysis with space/time models. Briefings in Bioinformatics 12, 41–51. (https://doi.org/10.1093/bib/bbq072)
	- PHYLUCE: Faircloth BC. 2016 PHYLUCE is a software package for the analysis of conserved genomic loci. Bioinformatics 32, 786–788. (https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btv646)
	- SeqKit: Shen W, Le S, Li Y, Hu F. 2016 SeqKit: A Cross-Platform and Ultrafast Toolkit for FASTA/Q File Manipulation. PLoS ONE 11, e0163962. (https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0163962)
      
%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export LANG=C.UTF-8
    export PERL5LIB=/opt/perl5/lib/perl5:$PERL5LIB
    export PATH=\
/opt/perl5/bin:\
/opt/gabbi/scripts:\
/opt/ucsc_tools:\
/opt/cactus/venv-cactus-v3.1.4/bin:\
/opt/phast/bin:\
/opt/maffilter/bin:\
/opt/cactus/bin:\
/opt/blast/bin:\
/opt/bbmap:\
/opt/miniconda3/bin:\
$PATH
    export PYTHONPATH=/opt/cactus/lib:$PYTHONPATH
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/cactus/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/bpp/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
    export LG_UTILS_PATH="/opt/omm_macse/UTILS"
    export LG_MAFFT="mafft"
    export LG_MUSCLE="muscle"
    export LG_PRANK="/opt/prank/bin/prank"
    export LG_MACSE="/opt/omm_macse/UTILS/macse_v2.08.jar"
    export LG_HMMCLEANER="/opt/omm_macse/UTILS/HMMcleanerV1_8_VR2/HMMcleanAA_VR.pl"
    export R_LIBS_USER=/opt/R/library
    export R_LIBS=/opt/R/library
    source /opt/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
    export BASH_ENV=/opt/etc/bashrc

%files
    main.sh                                   /opt/gabbi/main.sh
    config/help.txt                           /opt/gabbi/config/help.txt
    config/maffilter.optionfile               /opt/gabbi/config/maffilter.optionfile
    config/phylomera.conf                     /opt/gabbi/config/phylomera.conf
    utils/gabbi_functions.sh                  /opt/gabbi/utils/gabbi_functions.sh
    utils/defaults.sh                         /opt/gabbi/utils/defaults.sh
    utils/checkpoint.sh                       /opt/gabbi/utils/checkpoint.sh
    phases/01_cactus_alignment.sh             /opt/gabbi/phases/01_cactus_alignment.sh
    phases/02_conserved_loci.sh               /opt/gabbi/phases/02_conserved_loci.sh
    phases/03_cross_blast.sh                  /opt/gabbi/phases/03_cross_blast.sh
    phases/04_shr_extraction.sh               /opt/gabbi/phases/04_shr_extraction.sh
    phases/05_adding_genomes.sh               /opt/gabbi/phases/05_adding_genomes.sh
    phases/06_final_targeted_loci.sh          /opt/gabbi/phases/06_final_targeted_loci.sh
    scripts/clean_amas_partition.py           /opt/gabbi/scripts/clean_amas_partition.py
    scripts/drop_short_seq.py                 /opt/gabbi/scripts/drop_short_seq.py
    scripts/make_partition_from_probe2.py     /opt/gabbi/scripts/make_partition_from_probe2.py
    scripts/extract_chromosomes_from_maf.py   /opt/gabbi/scripts/extract_chromosomes_from_maf.py
    scripts/regroup_matches_from_blastn.py    /opt/gabbi/scripts/regroup_matches_from_blastn.py
    scripts/get_tiled_probes.py               /opt/gabbi/scripts/get_tiled_probes.py
    scripts/remove_flank.py                   /opt/gabbi/scripts/remove_flank.py
    scripts/phylomera_v0.8.3.sh               /opt/gabbi/scripts/phylomera_v0.8.3.sh
    scripts/merge_overlapping_seq_in_fasta.py /opt/gabbi/scripts/merge_overlapping_seq_in_fasta.py
    scripts/make_consensus_from_mafft_v3.R    /opt/gabbi/scripts/make_consensus_from_mafft_v3.R
    scripts/download_genomes_ncbi.sh          /opt/gabbi/scripts/download_genomes_ncbi.sh
    scripts/split_fasta.py                    /opt/gabbi/scripts/split_fasta.py
    scripts/run_BBMap.sh                      /opt/gabbi/scripts/run_BBMap.sh
    scripts/atram_blast.py                    /opt/gabbi/scripts/atram_blast.py
    scripts/atram_spades.py                   /opt/gabbi/scripts/atram_spades.py

%post -c bash
    # ===========================================================================
    # System dependencies
    # ===========================================================================
    apt-get update && apt-get upgrade -y
    apt-get install -y tzdata
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        wget curl git ca-certificates \
        build-essential cmake automake \
        python3 python3-dev python3-pip python3-venv \
        parallel \
        vim less \
	bzip2 rsync \
        libpcre3-dev libblas-dev liblapack-dev \
        cpanminus \
        openjdk-8-jre \
        jq
    
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive

    # ===========================================================================
    # Python packages
    # ===========================================================================
    pip3 install --no-cache-dir biopython==1.78
    pip3 install --no-cache-dir virtualenv

    # ===========================================================================
    # R 4.5 and packages
    # ===========================================================================
    # Add CRAN repository for R 4.5
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
	software-properties-common \
	dirmngr \
	gnupg \
	apt-transport-https

    # Add CRAN GPG key and repository
    wget -qO- https://cloud.r-project.org/bin/linux/ubuntu/marutter_pubkey.asc \
	| gpg --dearmor \
	| tee /usr/share/keyrings/r-project.gpg > /dev/null

    echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/r-project.gpg] \
	https://cloud.r-project.org/bin/linux/ubuntu jammy-cran40/" \
	> /etc/apt/sources.list.d/r-project.list

    apt-get update -y
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        r-base \
        r-base-dev \
	libcurl4-openssl-dev \
	libssl-dev \
	libxml2-dev

    # Install R packages
    mkdir -p /opt/R/library
    Rscript -e "
      install.packages(
	c('ape', 'stringr', 'igraph'),
	lib   = '/opt/R/library',
	repos = 'https://cloud.r-project.org',
	Ncpus = parallel::detectCores()
      )
    "

    # ===========================================================================
    # Tool installation
    # ===========================================================================

    # -- Cigar 0.1.3 : prebuild wheel to fix an error during th venv creation ---
    pip3 download --no-deps --no-binary :all: cigar==0.1.3 -d /tmp/cigar_dl
    cd /tmp && tar -xzf /tmp/cigar_dl/cigar-0.1.3.tar.gz && cd cigar-0.1.3

    # Neutralize ez_setup.py
cat > ez_setup.py << 'EOF'
def use_setuptools(*args, **kwargs):
    pass
EOF
    
    pip3 install build
    python3 -m build --wheel --outdir /tmp/cigar_wheel/

    # -- Cactus3.1.4 + Toil 7.0.0 -----------------------------------------------
    cd /opt
    wget https://github.com/ComparativeGenomicsToolkit/cactus/releases/download/v3.1.4/cactus-bin-v3.1.4.tar.gz
    mkdir /opt/cactus
    tar -xzf cactus-bin-v3.1.4.tar.gz -C /opt/cactus --strip-components=1
    rm cactus-bin-v3.1.4.tar.gz
    cd /opt/cactus
    git config --global --add safe.directory /opt/cactus

    virtualenv -p python3 venv-cactus-v3.1.4
    printf "export PATH=$(pwd)/bin:\$PATH\nexport PYTHONPATH=$(pwd)/lib:\$PYTHONPATH\nexport LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$(pwd)/lib:\$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\n" >> venv-cactus-v3.1.4/bin/activate
    source /opt/cactus/venv-cactus-v3.1.4/bin/activate
    python3 -m pip install -U setuptools pip wheel
    python3 -m pip install --no-index --find-links /tmp/cigar_wheel cigar
    python3 -m pip install -U .
    python3 -m pip install -U -r ./toil-requirement.txt
    

    # -- PHAST  (phastCons, phyloFit) -------------------------------------------
    mkdir /tmp/phast
    cd /tmp/phast
    wget https://github.com/CshlSiepelLab/phast/archive/refs/tags/v1.9.7.tar.gz
    tar -zxf v1.9.7.tar.gz
    mkdir /opt/phast
    mv phast-1.9.7/* /opt/phast/
    cd /opt/phast
    # fix an error with exp@@GLIBC_2.29
    sed -i '1s/^/link_libraries(m)\n/' CMakeLists.txt

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/phast
    cmake --build build
    cmake --install build

    # -- HmmCleaner -----------------------------------------------------------
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
	hmmer libssl-dev \
	libnet-ssleay-perl libio-socket-ssl-perl \
	libmoose-perl libmoosex-strictconstructor-perl \
	liblist-moreutils-perl
    mkdir -p /opt/perl5
    export PERL5LIB=/opt/perl5/lib/perl5
    cpanm --local-lib /opt/perl5 --force Test::Files
    cpanm --local-lib /opt/perl5 Bio::MUST::Core
    cpanm --local-lib /opt/perl5 Bio::MUST::Drivers
    cpanm --local-lib /opt/perl5 --force Bio::MUST::Apps::HmmCleaner
#    sed -i '1s|.*|#!/usr/bin/env perl|' /root/perl5/bin/HmmCleaner.pl

    # -- Maffilter 1.3.1 --------------------------------------------------------
    # Bio++ and eigen3
    apt-get install -y libeigen3-dev \
        libboost-all-dev \
        libbz2-dev
    for lib in bpp-core bpp-seq bpp-seq-omics bpp-phyl bpp-phyl-omics bpp-popgen; do
	git clone --branch v3.0.0 https://github.com/BioPP/${lib} /tmp/${lib}
	cmake -S /tmp/${lib} -B /tmp/${lib}/build \
	    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/bpp \
	    -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF
	cmake --build /tmp/${lib}/build -j$(nproc)
	cmake --install /tmp/${lib}/build
	rm -rf /tmp/${lib}
    done
    
    cd /opt
    git clone https://github.com/jydu/maffilter
    cd maffilter  
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-core [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-core/g' CMakeLists.txt
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-seq [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-seq/g' CMakeLists.txt
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-seq-omics [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-seq-omics/g' CMakeLists.txt
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-phyl [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-phyl/g' CMakeLists.txt
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-phyl-omics [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-phyl-omics/g' CMakeLists.txt
    sed -i 's/find_package(bpp-popgen [0-9.]*/find_package(bpp-popgen/g' CMakeLists.txt

    cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/maffilter -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/bpp .
    make install

    # -- Phyluce ----------------------------------------------------------------
    # Conda/miniconda
    mkdir -p /opt/miniconda3
    wget https://repo.anaconda.com/miniconda/Miniconda3-latest-Linux-x86_64.sh -O /opt/miniconda3/miniconda.sh
    bash /opt/miniconda3/miniconda.sh -b -u -p /opt/miniconda3
    rm /opt/miniconda3/miniconda.sh
    source /opt/miniconda3/bin/activate
    conda init --all

    # Phyluce
    mkdir /opt/phyluce
    cd /opt/phyluce
    wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/faircloth-lab/phyluce/v1.7.3/distrib/phyluce-1.7.3-py36-Linux-conda.yml
    conda tos accept
    conda env create -n phyluce --file phyluce-1.7.3-py36-Linux-conda.yml

    # -- BLAST+ 2.17.0+ ---------------------------------------------------------
    mkdir /tmp/blast
    cd /tmp/blast
    wget https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/blast/executables/blast+/LATEST/ncbi-blast-2.17.0+-x64-linux.tar.gz
    tar -zxf ncbi-blast-2.17.0+-x64-linux.tar.gz
    mkdir /opt/blast
    mv ncbi-blast-2.17.0+/* /opt/blast
    

    # -- IQ-TREE 3.0.1 ----------------------------------------------------------
    conda install -y bioconda::iqtree==3.0.1

    # -- BBMap (Sept 2022) ------------------------------------------------------
    cd /opt
    wget https://sourceforge.net/projects/bbmap/files/BBMap_39.77.tar.gz
    tar -xzf BBMap_39.77.tar.gz
    rm BBMap_39.77.tar.gz

    # -- SeqKit 2.9.0 -----------------------------------------------------------
    conda install -y -c bioconda seqkit

    # -- faToTwoBit -------------------------------------------------------------
    mkdir -p /opt/ucsc_tools
    wget -P /opt/ucsc_tools https://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/admin/exe/linux.x86_64/faToTwoBit

    # -- MAFFT ------------------------------------------------------------------
    conda install -y conda-forge::mafft

    # -- NCBI datasets CLI ------------------------------------------------------
    conda install -y -c conda-forge ncbi-datasets-cli

    # -- OMM_MACSE pipeline -----------------------------------------------------
    # These are fetched from OMM_MACSE_V12.02_sing_3.def

    mkdir /opt/omm_macse

    # Prank
    wget http://wasabiapp.org/download/prank/prank.linux64.170427.tgz
    tar -zxf prank.linux64.170427.tgz
    rm prank.linux64.170427.tgz

    git clone https://github.com/ranwez/MACSE_V2_PIPELINES.git /tmp/MACSE_V2_PIPELINES

    mv /tmp/MACSE_V2_PIPELINES/OMM_MACSE /opt/omm_macse
    mv /tmp/MACSE_V2_PIPELINES/UTILS /opt/omm_macse

    rm -rf /opt/omm_macse/OMM_MACSE/V*_FREEZED
    rm -rf /opt/omm_macse/UTILS/macse_v2.03.jar /opt/omm_macse/UTILS/macse_v2.05.jar /opt/omm_macse/UTILS/macse_v2.07.jar
    rm -rf /opt/omm_macse/OMM_MACSE/examples
    rm -rf /tmp/MACSE_V2_PIPELINES

    # -- aTRAM ------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Adapted script, cf: https://github.com/juliema/aTRAM/issues/321

    conda config --add channels defaults
    conda config --add channels bioconda
    conda config --add channels conda-forge

    git clone https://github.com/juliema/aTRAM.git /opt/atram
    sed -i '/juliema\/aTRAM/d' /opt/atram/environment.yml
    source /opt/miniconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh

    conda tos accept
    conda env create -n aTRAM -f /opt/atram/environment.yml

    /opt/miniconda3/envs/aTRAM/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir '/opt/atram[complete]'

    # Check aTRAM dependencies
    /opt/miniconda3/envs/aTRAM/bin/python -c "import Bio, psutil; print('aTRAM deps OK')"

    conda clean --tarballs -y

    # Apply changes to blast.py and spades.py
    for pydir in /opt/miniconda3/envs/aTRAM/lib/python3.*/site-packages/lib; do
        [ -d "$pydir" ] || continue
        cp /opt/gabbi/scripts/atram_blast.py "$pydir/blast.py"
        [ -d "$pydir/assemblers" ] && cp /opt/gabbi/scripts/atram_spades.py "$pydir/assemblers/spades.py"
    done

    # --- Other Phylomera dependencies ------------------------------------------
    conda install bioconda::seqkit
    python3 -m pip install -U amas

    # --- Make all tools executable ---------------------------------------------
    find /opt/gabbi \( -name "*.sh" -o -name "*.py" \) -exec chmod 755 {} \;
    chmod 777 /opt/ucsc_tools/faToTwoBit
    chmod 777 /opt/omm_macse/OMM_MACSE/*.sh
    chmod -R 777 /opt/omm_macse/UTILS/LGS_Fasta/*.sh
    chmod 777 /opt/miniconda3/lib/python3.13/site-packages/amas/AMAS.py
    chmod -R 777 /opt/atram
    chmod -R 777 /opt/miniconda3/envs/aTRAM/bin
    find /opt/miniconda3/envs/aTRAM/lib/python3.*/site-packages/lib \
        -name "*.py" -exec chmod 755 {} \; 2>/dev/null || true

%runscript
    #!/usr/bin/env bash

    # Handle --help before anything else
    for arg in "$@"; do
        if [[ "$arg" == "--help" || "$arg" == "-h" ]]; then
            cat /opt/gabbi/config/help.txt
            exit 0
        fi
    done

    exec /opt/gabbi/main.sh "$@"

